-- To-do 265 (quest-only loot): 504 creature loot rows for 17 quest items drop for every player instead of only for players
--   who need them, so players and bots fill their bags with items of quests they do not have.
-- Cause: our creature_loot_template stores a positive chance for rows that are quest-only in the references. The core gives a
--   quest-only drop only to a player with an incomplete quest that has the item as an item objective or as a source item.
-- Change: set the chance of these rows to the reference value with a negative sign (quest-only). Only items whose quest link
--   exists in our database (item objective in quest_objective, or ItemDrop in quest_template) are changed: 1274, 1529, 3082,
--   4616, 17326, 17327, 17328, 17422, 17502, 17503, 17504, 20384, 20858, 20875, 30809, 42108, 43089. Left unchanged on purpose:
--   23270 (Tainted Helboar Meat, no quest links it in any database; quest 9361 would lose its drop) and 5448 (no quest uses it).
-- Source: the SkyFire 5.4.8 world database (negative chance) and the Cataclysm Preservation world database (QuestRequired=1,
--   same size), compared per creature and item. Checked 14-11-2026.
